# Bare PLURAL definite article marking habitual weekday recurrence -- "les
# lundis" ("on Mondays"), mirroring French's ordinary way of stating a
# recurring weekday. Larousse/Grevisse: the plural article on a day-of-the-
# week noun reads habitually, while the singular ("le lundi") is ambiguous
# between "next Monday" and a habitual "on Mondays" and is deliberately
# excluded from this vocabulary so only the unambiguous plural fires here.
les
